course: dictionary
lesson: 6598
title: Noise
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A noise is a sound, often loud, unpleasant or unexpected. Noise without a is loud, unwanted sound in general, as in «There's too much noise». The word a tells you that the noise is one sound you can count.
explain: «She asks Daddy to make a noise.» Here make a noise means to produce a sound. Check by swapping in sound: «She asks Daddy to make a sound» still makes sense, so noise and sound are close in meaning here.
explain: «Making noise on a hike helps bears hear you coming and move away.» The clue is helps bears hear you. Noise here is a sound you make on purpose, and it works as a warning.
explain: «Noise-cancelling headphones listen to the noise and play the opposite wave.» They work best on steady droning noise, such as a low hum from a train or plane engine. Context tells you the word means a sound that is unwanted and steady, not just any sound.
fact: Noise is loud, messy or unwanted sound.
fact: Sound is made by vibrations. Loud noise can damage your hearing, so cover your ears in very loud places.
fact: Strange noises, like a smoke alarm beeping, can warn you of danger.
fact: In class, «keep the noise down» means be quieter.
fact: Useful phrases: «make a noise», «background noise» (quiet noise that stays in the background).
exercise: «She asks Daddy to make a noise.» What does make a noise mean here? | Put on a coat | *Produce a sound | Clean the kitchen | Sing a song
exercise: In class, «keep the noise down» means what? | *Be quieter | Sing louder | Stop talking forever | Dance around
exercise: Which noise could warn you of danger? | A soft pillow | *A smoke alarm beeping | A bowl of soup | A green leaf
test: Why do noise-cancelling headphones work best on steady droning noise? | Because droning noise is always very quiet | Because they can cancel any sudden bang | *Because they can cancel out a low, steady hum | Because they are made of wool
test: «Making noise on a hike helps bears hear you coming.» Why do hikers make noise? | To attract bears to the camp | To make the bears fall asleep | *To warn bears so they move away | To hear the bears singing
exam: Which word is a synonym for noise, meaning unwanted sound? | Colour | Taste | *Racket | Silence
